Now I understand the full picture. Let me look at the issue requirements once more and plan the work.

**Issue 25 requirements:**
1. A server that binds successfully upserts its `{poolDir, port, pid, startedAt}` entry in the registry
2. Relaunching the same pool updates the existing entry rather than duplicating it
3. A missing or corrupt registry file is recreated on write, never a boot failure
4. Registry reads prune entries whose pid is dead or whose pool directory no longer exists before returning
5. Registry-module test seam against temp registry paths using live and spare pids
6. Full test suite, typecheck, and build clean

