Issue 25 done. Summary:

- **`engine/fleet.ts`**: added `upsertFleetEntry` (upserts by poolDir, recreates a missing/corrupt registry on write, never a boot failure) and `readFleetEntries` (prune-on-read: drops dead pids and vanished pool dirs before returning). `readFleetEntry` now reads through the pruned list.
- **`engine/server.ts`**: `createPoolServer` resolves poolDir to an absolute path once, then upserts `{poolDir, port, pid, startedAt}` after a successful bind (lock → bind → register). Registration is best-effort so a registry write failure never takes down a bound console.
- **Tests**: `fleet.test.ts` covers entry shape, upsert, corrupt-file recovery, and prune-on-read against temp registry paths using live `process.pid` and spawned-reaped spare pids; a new `fleet registration` block in `server.test.ts` covers bind-upsert, relaunch-update, corrupt/absent recovery, and no-registration-on-failed-bind. All booting server tests now pass a temp `registryPath`, so the machine-wide registry is never touched by the suite.

All 177 tests, `tsc --noEmit`, and the UI build are clean. Committed as `ff3d0a8`.
